Z||000006||FieroKyle||11-21-2001||11:40 AM||||I am looking for rims on the Fiero. When I was looking through the rims, I told the guy jokingly that it would look good on my Buick ourtside. The buick has nice rims on it right now anyway. I want 14's because I don't want to get brand new tires for the Fiero because I just spent 800 on a set a few months agao. Since I only drive the Fiero as a second car and has 60,000 mile tires on it, it won't eat up tires that fast. Besides, I like 14''ss on a Fiero because I like "meat" on my tire. Not into low profile tires on a Fiero.<P>Also, how did not know that may be I had a Turbo optioned Buick Regal thats in the start of a complete restoration??? LoL   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Again no money is going to the Buick for I wants, only to keep it running. I plan on driving it right into the ground. I plan on saving my money for some good attention to the Fiero over the winter. Theres a bunch of goodies I want to put on it. This year I plan on just getting the looks of the car improved and keeping it mint. Other than lowering it and may be new rims, thats really the only major things that its gonna look different from stock. Then after that do a couple of touch up things and plan getting the performance end out of it. Besides, chicks don't care for performance, just a nice looking car with a CD player, lol. Well not really, my g/f likes performance of the Fiero. She liked it that it whipped on her friends Grand Prix which they made an attempt to pimp out, lol.<P>[This message has been edited by FieroKyle (edited 11-21-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by FieroKyle (edited 11-21-2001).]||||reg||1
